#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:2
msgid "``switch`` tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:4
msgid ""
"Much like a switch statement in many programming languages, a switch task "
"consists of a control task and a array of tasks to switch between. The "
"control task is run first, and its output is captured and matched against "
"the case option of each of the items in the switch array to determine which "
"one to run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:6
msgid ""
"This can be used to define a task that runs a different subtask depending on "
"which platform it is running on like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:8
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.build]\n"
"control.expr = \"sys.platform\"\n"
"\n"
"  [[tool.poe.tasks.build.switch]]\n"
"  case = \"win32\"\n"
"  cmd  = \"windows_build\"\n"
"\n"
"  [[tool.poe.tasks.build.switch]]\n"
"  cmd  = \"posix_build\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:20
msgid ""
"In the above example the control task is an :doc:`expression <expr>` that "
"checks the value of ``sys.platform``, and if running on windows it'll "
"execute :toml:`windows_build`, otherwise it'll fall back to the default case "
"(i.e. the switch item with no case option defined) and execute :toml:"
"`posix_build`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:24
msgid "Available task options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:26
msgid ""
"``switch`` tasks support all of the :doc:`standard task options <../"
"options>` with the exception of ``use_exec``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:28
msgid "The following options are also accepted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:30
msgid "**control** : ``str`` | ``dict``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:29
msgid "str | dict"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:31
msgid ""
"A **required** inline definition for a task to be executed to get the value "
"that will determine which case task to run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:33
msgid ""
"**default** : ``Literal[\"pass\", \"fail\"]`` :ref:`📖<Don't fail if there's "
"no match>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:32
msgid "Literal[\"pass\", \"fail\"] 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:34
msgid ""
"Setting ``default =  \"pass\"`` will make the task succeed even if no case "
"was matched to the value and there was no default case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:38
msgid "Multiple values per case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:40
msgid ""
"It is also possible to define multiple values for a single case option by "
"providing a array of values like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:43
msgid ""
"[[tool.poe.tasks.build.switch]]\n"
"case = [\"linux\", \"darwin\"]\n"
"cmd  = \"build\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:50
msgid "Don't fail if there's no match"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:52
msgid ""
"If all tasks in the switch array include a case value, but none of them "
"match the result of the control task then by default the switch task will "
"fail. You can instead configure the switch task to pass and simply do "
"nothing by providing the 'default' option like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:56
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.build-on-windows]\n"
"control.expr = \"sys.platform\"\n"
"default = \"pass\"\n"
"\n"
"  [[tool.poe.tasks.build-on-windows.switch]]\n"
"  case = \"win32\"\n"
"  cmd  = \"build\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:67
msgid "Switching on an environment variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:69
msgid ""
"Using an :doc:`expr <expr>` task makes it convenient to run a different task "
"depending on the value of an environment variable as in the following "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:71
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.check_number]\n"
"control.expr = \"int(${BEST_NUMBER}) % 2\"\n"
"\n"
"  [[tool.poe.tasks.check_number.switch]]\n"
"  case = \"0\"\n"
"  expr = \"f'{${BEST_NUMBER}} is even')\"\n"
"\n"
"  [[tool.poe.tasks.check_number.switch]]\n"
"  case = \"1\"\n"
"  expr = \"f'{${BEST_NUMBER}} is odd'\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:84
msgid "Using this task will look like the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:86
msgid ""
"$ BEST_NUMBER=12 poe check_number\n"
"Poe <= int(${BEST_NUMBER}) % 2\n"
"Poe => f'{${BEST_NUMBER}} is even')\n"
"12 is even\n"
"\n"
"$ BEST_NUMBER=17 poe check_number\n"
"Poe <= int(${BEST_NUMBER}) % 2\n"
"Poe => f'{${BEST_NUMBER}} is odd'\n"
"17 is odd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:100
msgid "Switching on a named argument"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:102
msgid ""
"You can also run a different task depending on the value of a named argument "
"as in the following example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:104
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.icecream]\n"
"control.expr = \"flavor\"\n"
"args = [\"flavor\"]\n"
"\n"
"  [[tool.poe.tasks.icecream.switch]]\n"
"  case = \"chocolate\"\n"
"  cmd  = \"make_chocolate_icecream\"\n"
"\n"
"  [[tool.poe.tasks.icecream.switch]]\n"
"  case = \"strawberry\"\n"
"  cmd  = \"make_strawberry_icecream\"\n"
"\n"
"  [[tool.poe.tasks.icecream.switch]]\n"
"  cmd  = \"make_vanilla_icecream\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:121
msgid "So running this task would look like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:123
msgid ""
"$ poe icecream --flavor chocolate\n"
"Poe <= flavor\n"
"Poe => make_chocolate_icecream\n"
"..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:132
msgid "Forwarding free arguments via ``$POE_EXTRA_ARGS``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:134
msgid ""
"Free arguments passed to a switch task are available as ``$POE_EXTRA_ARGS`` "
"and are inherited by the selected subtask. This makes it possible to forward "
"arbitrary extra arguments to whichever branch is executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/switch.rst:136
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`forwarding-free-arguments-via-poe-extra-args` section of the "
"args guide for details and examples."
msgstr ""
